{"name":"Candy Drop","hex":"#c25d6a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Crystallized sugar formed by boiling down sugar syrup.","Edible, sweet-tasting confectionery containing sugar, or sometimes artificial sweeteners, and often flavored with fruit, chocolate, nuts, herbs and spices, or artificial flavors."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook in or coat with sugar syrup.","To form into congelations or crystals, especially of sugar or syrup."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candy"},{"term":"drop","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small quantity of liquid, just large enough to hold its own rounded shape through surface tension, especially one that falls from a source of liquid.","A dose of liquid medicine in the form of a drop (sense 1)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Of a liquid: to fall in drops or droplets. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To fall (straight down) under the influence of gravity, like a drop of liquid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candy","blocks":[{"text":"Candy, also known as sweets and lollies, is a confection that features sugar as a principal ingredient. The category, sugar confectionery, encompasses any sweet confection, including chocolate or chewing gum. Sugar-glazed vegetables, fruit, or nuts are considered candied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Candy_in_Damascus.jpg/330px-Candy_in_Damascus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy","wikidata":"Q185583"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Japanese_confectionery_store_in_%22The_Great_Buddha_Sweet_Shop%22_from_Akizato_Rito%27s_Miyako_meisho_zue_%281787%29.jpg/500px-Japanese_confectionery_store_in_%22The_Great_Buddha_Sweet_Shop%22_from_Akizato_Rito%27s_Miyako_meis